1
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,700
Hey, I've been wondering
about something for a while.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,440
this stuffed animal hanging here,

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:11,780
what exactly is it?

4
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,020
Is it a tanuki?

5
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,400
Isn't it a red panda?

6
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,140
No matter how you look at it,
it's a raccoon, isn't it?

7
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,660
"Isn't it" what?

8
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,580
Wasn't this Reiko's?

9
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:25,240
Well, I just assumed it was Reiko-san's.

10
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,420
It's not, you know.

11
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,020
It was already here when
I came to this police box,

12
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,480
hanging right here.

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,640
Now that you mention it,
I think it's been here since way back.

14
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,480
Then it must be Terai-san's?

15
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,900
No, that's not it. I remember now.

16
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,860
It was here when I got my first posting here,
right after graduating.

17
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,300
Then could it be...

18
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,720
Chief Ohara's?

19
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:50,620
No way, that's impossible.
If it were, it would be too creepy.

20
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:57,620
Maybe it's the master who's been living in this police box since way,
way back.

21
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,580
Ryo-chan, you're so silly.

22
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:11,180
When you watch TV, turn on the
lights and sit farther away, okay?

23
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,340
Anyone without money, come to me.

24
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:29,100
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,380
Blue sky, white clouds.

26
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:43,020
It'll all work out eventually, right?

27
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:59,960
Anyone without work, come to me.

28
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,580
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

29
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:08,620
Look, it's burning!

30
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,000
The crimson sky too.

31
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:18,320
It'll all work out eventually, right?

32
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,600
You get it, right?

33
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,540
I get it, I get it.

34
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:27,460
Once you get it, shut up and follow me.

35
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:45,060
A Giant Athletic Competition
for a 100 Million Yen Prize

36
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,760
Good, it's finished.

37
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:56,240
You really are good with your hands, senpai.

38
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:59,340
Well, when it comes to making toy cars,
I'm the best in Japan.

39
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:04,860
The best in Japan, my foot!

40
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:13,060
It took me three whole days to make it, Chief.
That's cruel!

41
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:17,220
You idiot! You skipped work
for three days to make that?

42
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:19,060
Well that's...

43
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:22,760
Clean this up quickly and go on patrol.

44
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,640
Damn that Chief.

45
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:31,160
One day I'll stick my hand in
his ear and rattle his molars.

46
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,580
Hey!

47
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:47,640
What did you say?!

48
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:15,780
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

49
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:18,208
Strictly speaking, the ruined zaru soba,

50
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:20,903
the repair costs for the
broken motorcycle and truck,

51
00:04:20,953 --> 00:04:23,740
plus the antique shop's
damages and medical bills,

52
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:26,460
come to a total of 99,999,800 yen.

53
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:34,620
Why do I have to pay for damages when I'm the one who got hit by the motorcycle?
I'm the victim!

54
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,216
The investigation results are in:

55
00:04:36,266 --> 00:04:43,720
the accident started when this toy car you
threw in the park hit that dog right on the head.

56
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:52,700
Even so, after an accident like that, not even a scratch?
You really are one lucky bastard.

57
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:56,440
Anyway,
take responsibility and pay for the damages.

58
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:11,640
Nakagawa, please! There's no way I can pay back 100 million yen!
Just this once, I'm begging you, lend me 100 million yen. Even as a senior, 100 million yen is -

59
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:16,120
You've got pocket money, Nakagawa, right?
100 million yen, come on.

60
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,020
No way.

61
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:23,380
Besides, senpai, if you want 100 million yen,
there's a way to get it on your own.

62
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:26,480
What? How can I get it?

63
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:27,880
Here it is.

64
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,280
A giant athletic field?

65
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:35,340
The Nakagawa Group built it with all
its might on reclaimed land in Tokyo Bay.

66
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:38,040
It finally opens next month.

67
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:44,020
To celebrate, they're holding an athletic race
with a 100 million yen prize for the winner.

68
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,760
So if I win, I'd really get 100 million yen?

69
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:51,680
Well, we called for entrants from
across the country by postcard,

70
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:55,100
and we received over a million entries,
can you believe it.

71
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:59,480
Fifty pairs were chosen
from among them to compete.

72
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:03,460
If it's you, senior,
I can get you in as a special case.

73
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:04,159
I see.

74
00:06:04,209 --> 00:06:08,520
After all, it pays to have friends
like Onzō of the Nakagawa Group.

75
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:11,760
But this race requires pairs to enter,

76
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:14,880
so we need to find a partner
who's confident in their stamina.

77
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:17,700
Then, Nakagawa, join me.

78
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:20,300
I can't, since I'm the organizer.

79
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,160
I see, then.

80
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:27,240
What? You two are entering as a pair too?

81
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:29,400
The prize is 100 million yen, after all.

82
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:33,140
All those nights we stayed up
writing entry postcards were worth it.

83
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,585
That's the way it is.
Sorry, but I can't pair up with you.

84
00:06:36,635 --> 00:06:38,140
Well, don't take it personally.

85
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:40,197
Damn it,

86
00:06:40,247 --> 00:06:43,940
I figured it'd be one of those
two if I was going to team up.

87
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:45,349
Oh well,

88
00:06:45,399 --> 00:06:49,140
whoever my partner is, as long as
I can compete, we'll manage somehow.

89
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:54,740
W-why do I have to
enter some race like that?

90
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,517
It's all the Chief's fault.

91
00:06:56,567 --> 00:07:02,560
You went and broke the model car I made with such care,
and that's how this whole mess started.

92
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:08,180
What? It's your own fault for building
that kind of thing while on duty!

93
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,500
Sorry, Chief.

94
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:14,660
But on my measly salary,
there's no way I can pay 100 million yen.

95
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:17,180
All you have to do is form a pair with me,
that's all.

96
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:20,020
Leave the rest to me, Chief.

97
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:21,840
No way!

98
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:25,720
Partnering with you has never
once turned out well for me.

99
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,120
Find someone else.

100
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:30,260
Fine, then there's no helping it.

101
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:32,600
Are you sure, Ryotsu?

102
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:36,700
I'm going to rob a bank right
now and steal 100 million yen.

103
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:41,500
That would make the Chief a
former boss of a robber, though.

104
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,300
Well, it can't be helped.

105
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:50,060
Tomorrow's morning paper will print our photos side by side,
mine as the robber and the Chief's as his former boss, won't it?

106
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:53,460
Well then,

107
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,780
Wait, Ryotsu! Don't do anything rash!

108
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:56,960
I've already made up my mind.

109
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:58,440
But, Ryotsu...

110
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:02,480
There's no other way to get a huge sum like 100 million yen,
you know.

111
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:04,500
Please reconsider.

112
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:07,200
But it was you who turned
down this great chance,

113
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,820
wasn't it, Chief?

114
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,940
Please, Ryotsu, don't do that!

115
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:14,140
Not blessed with a good boss...

116
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:16,080
Is this the pitiful fate of a subordinate?

117
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,980
Fine, I'll enter, all right, Ryotsu?

118
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,540
Really, Chief?

119
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,940
I knew you'd do it, Chief!

120
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:28,060
Having a good boss really is wonderful,
isn't it?

121
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:31,660
Chief, now we're definitely
getting that 100 million yen!

122
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:32,600
Let's do it!

123
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:41,480
Welcome to the Nakagawa Giant Athletic
Field Opening Commemorative Race!

124
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:45,220
Today's athletic course
has three stages in total.

125
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:49,800
Each field has ingeniously
designed events prepared for you.

126
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:58,280
As expected, these are all pairs of physical
powerhouses who made it through a million applications.

127
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:02,100
But the ones competing with us for
the title are Volvo and his crew,

128
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:05,860
and the Komachi group, who'd abandon
their women for money, I suppose.

129
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:07,540
Chief!

130
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,460
You're already dead.

131
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:15,360
Just kidding!

132
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,880
You've forgotten what I did for you!

133
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:23,380
Hondara old man, why are you here?

134
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:26,960
To make the world aware of my
world's strongest Hondara dog,

135
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:35,620
I'm here to set up a South American branch.
Well, for that I sent in a million postcards.

136
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:41,120
We succeeded in getting three pairs entered.
The victory is ours!

137
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:47,560
Those lousy suckers hated it!
Now then, right away, stage one!

138
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,180
Please head to the survival game field.

139
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:58,940
What is this room?

140
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:02,880
Everything inside the dome
has been built to a giant scale.

141
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:07,880
For this room, we made the kitchen and living room giant-sized
for a survival game.

142
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:13,060
So the giant athletic course means an athletic course
done inside giant things?

143
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:15,820
So we're playing gun
battles inside this room?

144
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,800
That seems to be the idea.

145
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,900
Then, please choose your air guns first.

146
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,440
What kind of gun is this?

147
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:26,080
Do they really expect us to
shoot each other with these guns?

148
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:29,580
This dome was built for the
purpose of an athletic course.

149
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:32,640
To build up your stamina,
it has to be this big.

150
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:35,880
Running while carrying this
really does take stamina

151
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:39,720
Does it actually fire properly?

152
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,940
It's special BB pellets.

153
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,600
Since the pellets contain paint,

154
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:48,080
paint will stick to your clothes
the moment it hits your body.

155
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:50,400
So if you get paint on you, you're out?

156
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:51,500
That's right.

157
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:55,260
Once everyone has chosen their guns,
let's start the competition right away.

158
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:58,980
Now announcing the team divisions.

159
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:04,700
Bib numbers 1 through 25 are Team A,
and their territory is the living room.

160
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:10,980
Bib numbers 26 through 51 are Team B,
and their territory is the dining kitchen.

161
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:15,680
The team that has its empty cans
taken from its territory loses.

162
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:20,140
On the other side is Volvo,
who has military experience.

163
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:21,940
He's going to be a tough one.

164
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,920
Don't worry.

165
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,240
We've got me and you on our side, don't we?

166
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:29,200
Since we're on the same team,
let's join forces.

167
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:30,905
Alright,

168
00:11:30,955 --> 00:11:35,320
scatter to the spots I tell you to.

169
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:37,020
Alright, let's go.

170
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:59,460
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

171
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:01,680
If they set up a fixed gun, we're finished.

172
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:04,200
That heavy Bolmome means they won't move.
Is that the plan?

173
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,360
We have no choice but to
circle around and attack.

174
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:10,320
Wait, Ryotsu! On top of the bookshelf!

175
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:16,260
Whoa, whoa! If I'd gone out just now,
I'd have been an easy target.

176
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:19,120
Ryotsu, there's a sniper on your left. Move!

177
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,280
I know, I'm taking him out now!

178
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:22,640
Heavy

179
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:24,320
Chief, Pido on the right!

180
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:26,800
Alright, fire!

181
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,400
Ryotsu, I got one down!

182
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:33,560
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

183
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:34,487
It hurts...

184
00:12:34,537 --> 00:12:38,300
I forgot to make this gun blowback.

185
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,740
Yes, second hit too!

186
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:48,420
Looks like the enemy
team has stopped moving.

187
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,780
We'll break through the center,
so leave the rest to us!

188
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:52,340
Right!

189
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,860
From here on,

190
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:00,280
they won't get past us.

191
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,620
You bastards are breaking the rules!

192
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,240
We won't lose in a brawl!

193
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:20,040
Of course, the team with Volvo-san and
Sakonji-san has the advantage, right?

194
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:25,740
But once prize money is on the line, I bet Senpai
will win by any dirty trick he can, you know.

195
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:26,920
Yeah, that's true.

196
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,580
The game's just getting started.

197
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,480
I'm definitely going to
take that 100 million yen.

198
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,220
That's it!

199
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:52,540
They've surrounded us.

200
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,400
Play!

201
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:57,960
Yes!

202
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:01,560
Ryo, I'm tired, I can't move anymore.

203
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:05,500
Chief, we could always
just go rob a bank instead.

204
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,200
Th-that's not allowed!

205
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:07,800
Right?

206
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:09,654
Now then,

207
00:14:09,704 --> 00:14:13,360
if we take those guys out,
we can reach the empty cans!

208
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:21,620
Damn, I didn't expect him to be over there!

209
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:22,680
Alright!

210
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:27,920
Damn! He got underneath us!

211
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:33,300
Whaaat? Just now!

212
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,160
Me

213
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:42,540
Me... What a dirty trick to use!

214
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:43,840
But with this chance now,

215
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:46,140
Take this!

216
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:47,620
Ha-ha-ha!

217
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:50,740
Damn.

218
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:51,840
Alright, let's go.

219
00:14:51,840 --> 00:15:00,040
W-what's that?

220
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:31,100
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

221
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,140
Crap, I'm out of ammo!

222
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:35,240
Ew, even the cockroaches are giant!

223
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:37,720
Well, they're robots, though.

224
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:40,980
Even their repairs are programmed in,
you know.

225
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,680
Don't fly!

226
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,320
How about that!

227
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,860
Ryotsu, use this!

228
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:01,704
This can take care of
normal cockroaches, but

229
00:16:01,754 --> 00:16:02,880
Whatever happens, here goes!

230
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:07,660
Even though it's a robot...

231
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:09,780
Ryotsu, we got it!

232
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:12,960
Team B wins!

233
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:17,280
To think we'd be eliminated
in the first round...

234
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:19,860
My dream of buying up all
the victory figurines...

235
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:25,080
The second stage is a
maze made of giant sushi.

236
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:29,320
Of course, the sushi is real,
made with cutting-edge biotechnology.

237
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:34,300
The first four teams to skillfully make their way
through the maze and touch the flag on the central tower

238
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,220
will advance to the final field.

239
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:40,840
You know who got you this far, don't you?

240
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,860
That has nothing to do with it.

241
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:45,460
Yeah, from now on it's not
a team game anymore, right?

242
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:46,180
Bee.

243
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,380
You ungrateful bunch.

244
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:52,340
It's the size of one piece,
but it's definitely real.

245
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:55,180
They use biotechnology to
make something like this?

246
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:58,900
Climbing over the sushi is a foul
and will result in disqualification.

247
00:16:58,900 --> 00:17:00,420
Now then, ready!

248
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:06,340
This is pretty complicated

249
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:08,280
Damn it, I have no idea!

250
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:13,560
Ryotsu,
looks like you took the wrong path again.

251
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:17,000
Sōsui, I can see the goal past the octopus!

252
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,960
Straight ahead here, then?

253
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:22,780
Alright.

254
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,800
Either way, it's a living hell.

255
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:28,620
No, it's fine.

256
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,540
You're just eating it, aren't you!

257
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,260
Wow, what a clever move!

258
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,820
I'm going to do it that way too!

259
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:38,520
As long as we don't climb over them,
it's fine.

260
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:51,380
Eating their way through the sushi,
just like termites.

261
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:54,320
With those seniors,
they'd eat through a whole house

262
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:00,820
They're already way over there.

263
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:03,320
Four teams are up there!

264
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:05,340
Don't give up, it's too early.

265
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:06,900
Here we go!

266
00:18:13,180 --> 00:18:15,560
I'm going to be the one on top!

267
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:18,820
You Hontarō old geezer! I won't let you!

268
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,120
Damn it!

269
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,320
Got you!

270
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:25,340
Hey, let go! The top spot is mine!

271
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,840
Take this, last one!

272
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,120
Damn it!

273
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:38,140
Move aside, you Hontarō old geezer!

274
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:41,160
Excuse me, caveman!

275
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,740
Hontarō-ken takes first and second place!

276
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,940
Yes! We got third place!

277
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,480
Fourth place is ours!

278
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,480
No way, we can't make it in time now.

279
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:58,380
Nobody's getting that last gap from me!

280
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,020
Out of my way!

281
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,440
Move! Move!

282
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:01,460
Bakekuru gun show!

283
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,660
Yes! We got fourth place!

284
00:19:05,260 --> 00:19:08,440
When money's involved,
he's truly terrifying.

285
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:11,240
Now, the final stage.

286
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:15,500
The remaining four teams will compete
in a tournament of giant sports showdowns.

287
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:19,700
Now, the first match of
the table tennis semifinals.

288
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,419
Ryotsu and Ohara's pair
versus Ono and Seishō's pair,

289
00:19:22,469 --> 00:19:24,200
Begin the match!

290
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:28,140
Here we go! Ready, set, hoi!

291
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:30,400
Alright, got it!

292
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:36,480
Heh, the enemy's teamwork is terrible.

293
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:38,440
Komachi, we'll take this match, right?

294
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:38,720
Yeah.

295
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,200
Alright, that's match point!

296
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:56,200
Ryotsu, this is the end.
There's no way to make a comeback now.

297
00:19:58,140 --> 00:19:59,240
Building 5 has been... all along.

298
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:00,560
I'm not joking, you know.

299
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:03,400
We've got the hang of it now,
so the real game starts here.

300
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,360
You still haven't given up?

301
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:07,660
I'll turn this around, I promise.

302
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,360
Here it goes!

303
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,380
Leave it to me.

304
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:13,280
I put backspin on it.

305
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:15,540
When did you learn a trick like that?

306
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:17,160
Alright, counterattack!

307
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:20,480
There it is

308
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:22,980
Okay

309
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:30,380
Okay, from here it's sudden death.
First to score a point wins.

310
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:33,480
So who serves? Let's do rock-paper-scissors.

311
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,700
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

312
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,820
If we get the serve, it's as good as won.

313
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:43,640
Naoko, watch out for the spin serve!

314
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:47,320
No way they'll hit it that easily.

315
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,400
Kimutaku.

316
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,260
Where? Where?

317
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:52,300
Now!

318
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:56,800
Game set!

319
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:59,040
Ryotsu and Chief Ohara's pair wins!

320
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,140
Dirty!

321
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:03,600
A tricky serve is just
common sense in ping-pong.

322
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:06,960
Even though he's on our side,
he's really a dirty guy.

323
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:09,840
The final is a bowling showdown.

324
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:13,280
Then please begin with
Honda's Team A going first.

325
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:16,360
They really do have holes in them

326
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:17,400
Right!

327
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:19,340
Here I go!

328
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:21,640
Gutter!

329
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:22,440
It won't come out!

330
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:30,020
Aaaaah, if that's a strike,
then you're the old man!

331
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:33,660
But I've figured out the approach, I have!

332
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,580
Aaaaaah!

333
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,920
It's hard since I can't see in front of me.

334
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:51,200
Ryotsu, the situation has suddenly changed!

335
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:53,140
If we get a spare or better, we can win!

336
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:57,700
You haven't gotten a
single spare yet, though.

337
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:58,760
No way, no way.

338
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:01,460
Shut up, I'll finish it with a strike!

339
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:04,020
Yaaah!

340
00:22:09,060 --> 00:22:26,720
!

341
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:32,560
You can't get a spare like that.

342
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:33,900
Is this it?

343
00:22:33,900 --> 00:22:36,100
This is where the real fight begins!

344
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,020
There's one!

345
00:22:37,700 --> 00:22:38,220
There!

346
00:22:38,220 --> 00:22:41,480
What?

347
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:45,900
A little more to the right!

348
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,240
Yes!

349
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:59,380
Looks like even our last
strategy was for nothing.

350
00:22:59,380 --> 00:23:00,980
The championship is ours.

351
00:23:05,340 --> 00:23:06,700
100 million yen.

352
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:10,980
It fell.

353
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:14,540
Good job, Ryo-san!

354
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:16,580
What tenacity!

355
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:17,600
We lost.

356
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:26,520
Well, aren't you lucky, Ryo-chan.
You managed to pay back 100 million yen.

357
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,300
That was a magnificent battle.

358
00:23:28,460 --> 00:23:30,760
Though my body's a wreck because of it.

359
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:32,820
Alright, it's done.

360
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:35,740
Chief!

361
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:38,920
How many times do I have to tell you,
you idiot?

362
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:40,720
I'll hold on to this.

363
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,320
Chief, come on!

364
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:43,360
No way.

365
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,500
Give it back.

366
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:44,960
Let go.

367
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:45,380
There.

368
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:45,880
Wait.

369
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:47,580
Let go already!

370
00:23:47,700 --> 00:23:48,340
Let go.

371
00:23:48,420 --> 00:23:49,640
Come on, please let go.

372
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:59,420
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!

373
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:02,820
Paying back 100 million yen now?
That's brutal!

374
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:20,340
The day after the rain,
as if someone was calling

375
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:27,200
Walking while looking back,
hand in hand with Mom

376
00:24:28,060 --> 00:24:34,340
That strange feeling I had back then

377
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:39,600
So on the tiles of the arcade street

378
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:45,420
I walked only on the black ones

379
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:51,560
Everyone was a child once

380
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:53,700
But everyone forgets

381
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:57,660
Politicians with their self-important faces

382
00:24:57,660 --> 00:25:01,000
And the aunties with the blue eyeshadow too

383
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,980
Try turning

384
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:06,580
at that corner

385
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:11,760
I'll get to see everyone, everyone!

386
00:25:12,340 --> 00:25:16,380
Over there is Kameari,

387
00:25:17,300 --> 00:25:19,700
well, surely it's Kameari.

388
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:24,960
Everyone, come on over to our town!

389
00:25:26,140 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you.

390
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,460
Look, look, Ryotsu.

391
00:25:31,460 --> 00:25:33,960
Just because it's a festival,
don't get too carried away.

392
00:25:35,260 --> 00:25:38,500
That pickpocket I caught back in the day,
the bitterness of it...

393
00:25:39,100 --> 00:25:41,420
Didn't you go straight?

394
00:25:41,420 --> 00:25:43,460
What happened to your promise to me?

395
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:47,180
Count on you at the next festival, okay?

